Starting a series of major updates of ModEM stable. Initially, pushing out the bug fixes. This version includes a new, complete set of configure scripts 
for all the other extensions that are coming up.
Some minor but annoying bugs are fixed:

1) Workaround for the type mismatch errors in MPI_declaration.f90 (MPI_pack and MPI_unpack) with the newer versions of GCC. The reason for these is that 
calling include 'mpif.h' does not allow for flexible type passing into subroutines. Instead, we should be using an MPI module. However, that will require 
more substantial compatibility changes. For now, included an -fallow-argument-mismatch argument in the configures files & makefiles to turn these errors 
into warnings. Everything still works.

2) Workaround for an annoying issue with the Intel compiler where it wraps output lines in the data file to 80 chars, making the output data file headers 
unreadable and unusable. This is now fixed (primarily by opening the file with recl=4096 argument). Works in Intel and GFortran without issues. 

