r629 | donghao | 2022-07-06 00:06:46 -0600 (Wed, 06 Jul 2022) | 50 lines

A few updates for the solver/MPI modules prior to the major update for GPU
solvers, people who are using CPU-only calculations can (hopefully) cling to 
this version for some time, in case my GPU update leads to some turmoil in
other part of the code.   

3D_MT/FWD/solver.f90 
3D_MT/FWD_SP/solver.f90 
3D_MT/FWD_SP2/solver.f90 
3D_MT/FWD_SPETSc2/solver.f90 

added a long overdue "working" TFQMR solver for all SP methods - 
this is mainly for the SP2/SPETSc2 version as the system matrix in CCGD is
no longer symmetric - the old QMR method will need the transpose of CCGD,
which is not saved in current set-up to reduce the memory consumption. 
This leads to two extra transpose operations in a QMR iteration, which slows
down the calculation.  
also omits an unnecessary SPMV operation in the BiCG code (for all FWD
methods). Should save some time for BiCG iterations, also. 

3D_MT/FWD/EMsolve3D.f90 
