for cartesian code, integer(8) for spherical code in the gridelements version - not good for trying to use the files!)
Also, added some grid error checking on input.

2)  UserCtrl.f90 changed to add fwdCtrl input file to most sensitivity tests.

3)  Jmult segmentation fault in SP fixed by passing the interior edges only to Div in FWDsolve3D in EMsolve3D.f90.
Note that passing s(EDGEi) directly to Div (bypassing a temporary si complex vector) also causes the optimized version 
of the Intel compiled program to produce a segmentation fault. Not at all sure why, but it just took me hours to locate 
so won't do that again.

4)  COMPILER BUG FIX: ifort (IFORT) 19.0.4.233 20190416 produced a segmentation fault with SP2 only (not with SP!)
    at the first encounter of the line "B%val(j1:j2) = A(i)%val" in BlkDiag_Cmplx in module spOpTools.f90.
    Something to do with vectorization, since this doesn't occur in debug mode. Rewritten to use a loop
    with error checking, for now. This is most likely a temporary fix that could be eliminated later.
    Should not present a problem: this is only done once at the beginning. Note: error checking not necessary.
         !B%val(j1:j2) = A(i)%val
         do j = 1,size(A(i)%val)
            if (isnan(real(A(i)%val(j)))) then
                write(0,*) 'ERROR: NaN in BlkDiag_Cmplx for i=',i,' and j=',j
            endif
            B%val(j1+j-1) = A(i)%val(j)
         enddo

