3D_MT/SolnSpace.f90
    fixed a bug when b%allocated== true but b%b(iTx)%allocated == false
    in create_rhsvector subroutine.
    well, normally this should not happen at all -
    this is more like a side effect when a dummy comb(b) is assigned 
    to one of the workers (non-leader) in a mpi subgroup. let's say after a
    REGROUP command, that worker becomes a leader. In this case the dummy comb
    has to be replaced by a real rhsvector. This could generate an error as 
    the dummy comb is not yet allocated (but treated like one as the programme
    only checked if b%allocated == true). 
3D_MT/FWD_SPETSc2/EMsolv3D.f90
