r570 | anya | 2019-07-02 20:15:03 -0600 (Tue, 02 Jul 2019) | 138 lines

A trivial but important and disruptive code reorganization. MPI modules/subroutines/variables have been renamed to no longer violate the MPI protocol.

Since modules (rather than subroutines) actually need to be renamed, there are all the dependencies that need to be tracked down, and all Makefiles need to be recreated. Since we are doing this anyway now with the introduction of two new modules (INVcore.f90 and LBFGS.f90), this seems to be a good time to do this.

Specifically, I renamed:

MPI_main.f90 -> Main_MPI.f90
MPI_sub.f90 -> Sub_MPI.f90
MPI_declaration.f90 -> Declaration_MPI.f90

Also, subroutines

MPI_constructor -> constructor_MPI
MPI_destructor -> destructor_MPI

I may have missed some other names to rename, but this addresses most of it. All other changes may be done without a major renaming and reorganization, unless and until we employ Fortran2003 with OOP. The code still compiles and runs in parallel.

We will need to also do this to stable at some point, but since that would be disruptive, I suggest we combine it with other major changes in the future.

I have created a CONFIG directory like we used to have in the trunk, and committed that. I have removed the Configure files from the root directory of ModEM; please feel free to revert any of them if you need them, but place them in the CONFIG now. You will need to use the Configure files to remake the makefiles before anything works for you again. It's good that we're going that now when people are actively working on the code! There is a good chance that it will go smoothly.

Finally, I have added some preliminary spherical coordinate modules for my own convenience.

NOTE: 2D parallel is currently broken in stable-. This isn't because of the renaming changes, but because of the reference to EdgeLength and FaceArea elements in Main_MPI (these aren't defined for 2D). I think these references are my fault and they need to be replaced with something substantially more elegant. Hopefully this will get fixed when the MPI gets reworked.

Email correspondence on the renaming issue is attached below for reference.




-------- Forwarded Message --------
Subject: 	Re: Re: [EXTERNAL] MAP with MoD3DMT
Date: 	Sun, 9 Jun 2019 12:03:03 +0800
From: 	董浩 <donghao@cugb.edu.cn>
To: 	meqbel <meqbel@modem-geophysics.com>
CC: 	anna kelbert <akelbert@usgs.gov>, gary egbert <egbert@coas.oregonstate.edu>


Hi Naser,


The problem is not with a particular compiler (or at least the MPI works fine for me with gfortran, ifort and Portland). So far it is only a potential issue as it violates the naming protocol of MPI and may cause confusion (with some auto-optimization schemes or profiling software). I guess we just need to take the precaution and change those names.


Cheers,

Hao


