    Cc: Naser Meqbel <meqbel@modem-geophysics.com>, Gary Egbert <egbert@coas.oregonstate.edu>
    Subject: Re: [EXTERNAL] MAP with MoD3DMT

    Hi Anna (and All) -

    In theory, the compiler actually doesn’t know about whether an MPI_ subroutine is from the MPI lib or not. As long as there are source codes, it will try optimizing the computation - the "practical" performance will not be different (I believe). The problem (with some profiler softwares, for example) is you don’t know if the optimization works or not. 

    Sorry, I must admit that I knew the naming issue before (I think I mentioned it to Gary once). I am more than happy to see it fixed. And moving the MPI to the end of the name would simplify the procedure. But I would hear Naser’s input first. 

    BTW, there are also some variables that start with MPI_. These should also be modified, as MPI reserves some names for certain usage (e.g. MPI_COMM_WORLD).  


    Cheers, 
    Hao

    P.S. I fixed a typo in the LBFGS module in stable- (wasn’t there in old ModEMsp). Now -I LBFGS should work “like a QN method”. Should be 50% faster than the stock CG as it only use 1 FWD and 1 TRN per iteration (CG can benefit from the same trick). You are welcomed to try it . 

