Major code modification that aims to include all of the updates from Hao Dong's sparse matrix (SP/SP2 and PetSc/PetSc2) that are relevant to the matrix-free code. 

This is only the first step towards that goal. It does not yet include the new two-layer MPI module. The updates in this commit are limited to:

1) Adding the optional LBFGS inversion code. This was accomplished by creating the new INVcore.f90 module that contains the func/gradient/Cd/Cm/printf that are
   generic to all inversion codes (in theory!) and using that module in both NLCG.f90 and LBFGS.f90. DCG.f90 is left intact for now, needs a more substantial 
   cleanup. Not done yet: new module not tested, UserCtrl.f90 not updated with relevant documentation (which is not found in Hao's codes).

2) NLCG module: lineSearchWolfe added as an option. NLCG logic edited by Hao is not yet incorporated. Requires more thought.

3) BICG linear solver added to 3D_MT/FWD/solver.f90. Option to use it not yet created.

4) info=0 added to 3D_MT/FWD/Mod3d/WSfwd1Dmod.f90 Solve1D function. Not sure why it's needed! Doesn't seem to break anything.

5) ModelParamToNode function added to 3D_MT/modelParam/ModelMap.inc and the corresponding Cell2Node function added to 3D_MT/GridCalc.f90. Will probably not work 
   for spherical coordinates out-of-the-box. Needs thinking and updating. To be used in a modified system of equations with node based scaling, but not used here.

6) DataIO module: tiny update to create a public interface for deall_fileInfo. This has now replaced the outdated "deall_datafile_info" that was used in the main
   program Mod3DMT.f90 to deallocate user-specific data file information. Now, embedded this call in deallGlobalData() that's called at the end of the program.

7) Master_job_stop_message now only used at the end of the program. Seems unnecessary to call it earlier. This is consistent with the latest stable version, 
   but distinct from the version that was in SP/SP2.

8) Added LBFGS to Mod3DMT.f90. Added back the writing of the header for JT_multi_Tx_vec.

9) Makefile updated using the configure script: ./Configure.3D_MT.GFortran Makefile3d release

Other purely formatting changes (for consistency between the two versions) in:

modelOperator3D.d90
solver.f90
Mod3DMT.f90

Everything compiles. Next step: testing.

