The only known bug is in Stest for 2D_MT: sparse2full_rhsVector doesn't work yet, so Stest cannot be run. Not a big deal and can be easily fixed when and if it is ever needed.

Before we can use the new BC input functionality, CHECK POLARIZATION INDEX IN RHS IO TO MAKE SURE THAT MODES ARE NOT GETTING MIXED UP. At present, everything runs but the impedances are different if you "compute" the BC, then read it in.

NEED TESTING:

NestedEM
MPI inversion
CSEM & DC
Global

I do not believe that any of these should be broken by my changes, but I have not tested them explicitly (yet). Will do that next. In the meanwhile, committing the code to the SVN to save changes. In general, it's got to be an improvement over all previous versions. Once I've tested the NestedEM and MPI inversion, will also propagate these changes to stable.

Joint inversion needs to be completely rewritten anyway - would be easy to clean up, but this would be scope creep at this point.

Spherical coordinate version has not been included yet. This version is still fully matrix-free and requires no additional storage.
All of these experiments are still in the semiglobal branch. The only exception is the inclusion of grid element matrices, stored in GridCalc - which in fact were already there in the previous version of the trunk. It seems very worthwhile to include the grid element matrices and the corresponding logic in this version, even though it is still purely Cartesian. With that modification, code maintenance (adding new features from other branches) will be much easier. Seems like we're not losing much by doing so but it does slightly increase the memory requirements. (Only slightly, because the grid elements only need to be stored once and do not need to be duplicated for every frequency and mode like the EM soln, for example.) 

  !!!!!!!>>>>>>>>> block of precomputed grid elements (public)
  !!!!!!!>>>>>>>>> initialized in ModelDataInit to accommodate
  !!!!!!!>>>>>>>>> for potential on-the-fly grid modification
  type(rvector), public     :: V_E, l_E, S_E ! edges (primary)
  type(rvector), public     :: V_F, l_F, S_F ! faces (dual)
  type(rscalar), public     :: V_N, V_C ! nodes and cells

However, these grid elements are still unused in sg_diff_oper.f90 and modelOperator3d.f90 computations. Doing so increased the code run time by 20% relative to stable. Need to optimize before inclusion.

Sparse matrix and PetSc versions should be automatic beneficiaries of these improvements, but there can easily be inconsistencies between some changes that I've made, and the alternative file versions in these distributions. Will work on that next, but after further clean up of source/BC input and usage.

What about 2D_ANIS and 3D_CSEM? Are these still active? Should they be maintained?

