r479 | anya | 2014-07-15 18:27:24 -0600 (Tue, 15 Jul 2014) | 34 lines

This is a working version that has major and minor fixes but no major changes compared to Naser's big update.

Global fixes:

Temporarily reverted UTILS/elements.f90 module to rev 453. The changes implemented in semiglobal
apparently completely break the global code, both forward modeling and adjoint.
The "correct" version of the code (e.g., this one, also r449-464) give the numbers
Total derivative test based on Taylor series [f(m0+dm) ~ f(m0) + df/dm|_{m0} x dm]
  f(m0+dm) - f(m0):   -5.212222    
  df/dm|_{m0} x dm:  -0.1050722E-02
(which is of course also incorrect and needs to be debugged! - but at least the inversion sort of works).
With the new elements module the answers, for the same l6m3 C responses example, were
  f(m0+dm) - f(m0):   -6919.008
  df/dm|_{m0} x dm:    1603.778
So, both amplitudes and signs completely wrong!!!!! Need to be very carefully investigated
before the new elements module can be used.
Also, no need to have nPol attribute in EARTH/SolnSpace.f90. This is reverted.

Mod3DMT:

Updates include corrected GridCalc modules (which are not used for any computations in this version
of the code!) and generalized I/O routines for sg_vectors and sg_scalars which allow both ascii
and binary types of output.

Finally, this includes some gfortran-friendly syntax changes.

The changes up to this version, including Kristina's fixes for apparent resistivities and phase tensors,
should most definitely be propagated to stable asap.

However, before I go this, I will uncomment the two lines that got commented out in writeVec_modelParam_binary,
as this would affect output for sensitivity matrices. Next commit will do that.

*This version has been tested to run the NLCG inversion for 3D_MT, joint 3D_EM and global.*

