r401 | anya | 2012-07-13 14:28:16 -0600 (Fri, 13 Jul 2012) | 40 lines

Important additions to global code: everything is now implemented to run forward models with tidal 
forcing (inversion should also work but wasn't tested). The code is now running with the M2 tidal 
source; results should now be correct - after fixing a scaling bug - but since the code is still 
running I can't tell; there might still be bugs remaining. Global *is* working correctly for 
external sources in this release.

Problem: in implementing this addition, I realised that I needed a bunch of basic operators that 
were never required before. For example, multiplication by rhoF instead of l_F rho_F (S_E)^-1 that 
previously existed (needed to output electric fields E = rho_F J).
More importantly, also need the operators l_F and (S_F)^-1. Other elemental operators that exist 
such as l_E and (S_E)^-1 need to be cleaned up from using wrappers to the original global forward 
solver. So overall, a detailed careful rewrite is finally necessary.

I made a quick shortcut to ensure that the program works now for the tidal stuff. I will now (or 
maybe soon, after the EMIW in Australia) start with this version and rewrite all of the elemental 
operators, with the idea that these can also be reused in the MT code.

The equation for tides (in T/s) looks like
[(S_E)^-1 C^T l_F] rho_F [(S_F)^-1 C l_E] h + i\omega\mu_0 h = [(S_E)^-1 C^T l_F] rho_F Js,
where Js = sigma_F (v x B). Rho and sigma cancel out to get
[(S_E)^-1 C^T l_F] rho_F [(S_F)^-1 C l_E] h + i\omega\mu_0 h = [(S_E)^-1 C^T l_F] (v x B)_F.

So (v x B) on faces is the sparse source input to the code. Need to be careful because B in IGRF 
is normally in nT, and the tidal velocities are normally given as tidal transport, depth 
integrated. Need to convert B to SI units (multiply by 1e-9) and compute v by dividing by depth.

We can write this equation as
(V_E)^-1 [l_E C^T (S_F)^-1] V_F rho_F [(S_F)^-1 C l_E] h + i\omega\mu_0 h = (V_E)^-1 [l_E C^T (S_F)^-1] V_F (v x B)_F

Here, (S_F)^-1 C l_E is the correct discrete curl operator, and l_E C^T (S_F)^-1 is its transpose.
Then, (V_E)^-1 [l_E C^T (S_F)^-1] V_F = (S_E)^-1 C^T l_F is the full adjoint in the dual vector space.

So, we need:
(S_E)^-1 C^T l_F - adjoint curl - also to compute the RHS for tidal FWD;
(S_F)^-1 C l_E - curl - also to compute and output current densities J from magnetic field strength H;
rho_F - mapping from cells to faces - also to compute E from J.

Will now save the working version and try to clean up and make all the changes without breaking 
it. Hmm. Sounds like a week of debugging, but it's pretty inevitable at this point.

