r326 | anya | 2011-03-31 16:30:22 -0600 (Thu, 31 Mar 2011) | 35 lines

Updating to trunk revision 325.

FIXES:  2D and 3D MT should now work with gfortran compiler (segmentation faults fixed);

MAJOR CHANGES: The covariance has been rescaled, so that we no longer get unreasonable conductivity
variations when the covariance is applied several times. The covariance file means
the same thing as before, but the resultant model perturbations now have different magnitude
(the "rough" model has bigger magnitude variations than the "smooth" model).

With the new covariance, the default damping parameter and line search step had to
be adjusted. I used this opportunity to scale the penalty functional as follows:

P(m) = (d-f(m))^T C_d^{-1} (d-f(m)) / N_d + lambda * (m-m_{prior})^T C_m^{-1} (m-m_{prior}) / N_m

where N_d is the number of real data values and N_m is the number of model parameters.
Now, lambda = 1 means that we are giving equal weighting to the data misfit and the model norm,
so this weighting gives a more intuitive feel to NLCG algorithm; the parameters should now be
independent of the relative model and data set sizes.

I also added an additional line to the inverse configuration file to regulate the adjustment
of the damping parameter lambda; an example configuration file will now look like this.

Model and data output file name    : Example
Initial damping factor lambda      : 1.
To update lambda divide by         : 10.
Initial search step in model units : 100.
Restart when rms diff is less than : 2.0e-3
Exit search when rms is less than  : 1.05
Exit when lambda is less than      : 1.0e-4
Maximum number of iterations       : 120

All this affects the user significantly, since the starting values of the damping parameter lambda
and the initial line search step alpha need to be adjusted to match the new covariance and penalty
functional scaling. The examples will soon be updated to reflect these changes.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
r325 | anya | 2011-03-31 16:12:38 -0600 (Thu, 31 Mar 2011) | 23 lines

MINOR FIXES to enable using the code with gfortran.

Previously, the 2D and 3D codes produced segmentation faults at run time 
when compiled with gfortran. Two reasons:
1. gfortran is very peculiar about deallocation; it's not enough to check
that the array is associated to be able to deallocate. Fixed by using
the allocated logical variable whenever possible.
2. in a = b, gfortran complains if size(a) /= size(b); other compilers
just take the first few elements of b is a is smaller. Fixed.

Hopefully this shouldn't affect the program behaviour with other compilers.

Use the following Macro-Defs to compile with a newer version of gfortran:

# ------------------Macro-Defs--------------------- 
include Makefile.local 
OBJDIR = ./objs/3D_MT/GFortranDebug F90 = 
gfortran
FFLAGS = -g -fbacktrace -fbounds-check -ffree-line-length-none
MPIFLAGS = -cpp
MODULE = -fintrinsic-modules-path $(OBJDIR)
LIBS = -lblas -llapack

