Creating a STABLE branch from trunk revision 298: up to date 2D and 3D MT + MPI with relatively clean examples and a user guide. Also has the draft of the paper, as submitted.

Here is what you should know before updating your code to this release:

1. This is a STABLE and the most current version of ModEM. The examples have been cleaned up and tested, 
and a user guide has been added in doc/userguide/.

2. This is a MAJOR UPDATE from any previous version you had. Specifically, the format for the data file has been changed. 
This version is INCOMPATIBLE with all the previous versions. Only update if you wish to switch to the new data format.

3. The functionality of the code has NOT been changed substantially from the previous versions, except that
the capability for missing data has been added with this release. It has NOT been tested. See User Guide.

4. The old data format WILL NOT BE SUPPORTED anymore.

Your old data files can be easily converted to the new format with Matlab scripts provided in matlab/ioAscii/.
There are scripts (writeZ_old2list_2D.m and writeZ_old2list_3D.m) that will read your old format and convert it 
to the new list format. Since the old format didn't store the geographic site locations, in some cases it may
be advisable to recreate your files directly with the addition of this information.

The scripts readZ_3D.m and writeZ_3D.m will read and write the NEW data format from now on. They use the same 
Matlab data structure as before, so all your Matlab scripts that use them (if any) should still work. Same for 2D.

Old read and write scripts have been renamed to readZ_3D_old.m and writeZ_3D_old.m, and can still
be used (except writeZ_3D_old.m should no longer be needed!). Same for 2D.


