r283 | naser | 2010-11-23 12:00:37 -0700 (Tue, 23 Nov 2010) | 25 lines

Major Changes:
Because now we are parallelizing over transmitters and modes for the 3D MT case (and other possible applications that require two source polarizations), major changes have been affected:
- MPI/MPI_main.f90:
    In the new version of this module, the Master sends one transmitter index and polarization index (if required) to each Worker. The worker call directly fwdsolve (for the forward modeling) and solveSens (for both JmultT and Jmult). However, before calling one of this subroutines in ForwardSolver.f90, the Workers change (if required) number of polarizations and the polarization index of e solution. This is done in MPI_sub, where two small subroutines are existing: one to return nPol_MPI and one to change e solution.
After editing e solution (if required) and calling i.e. fwdsolve the Worker send back to the Master one solution corresponds to one polarization (in case of two polarizations). The Master collects all solutions for all transmitters and possibly all polarizations in eAll. Afterwards, the Master computes the model responses (in case of Forward modeling). The same procedure is done for JmultT and jmult, however, while the Master sends the transmitter and mode indices, it must send also the the background solution for one transmitter (both modes) to the corresponding Worker.

- MPI/MPI_sub.f90:
     As described above, MPI_sub contains two new subroutine: one to read (from e solution) or to set nPol_MPI and one to edit e solution (if required). In case that we have only one polarization (i.e 2D MT), nPol_MPI is set to 1 and the two lines that edit e solution can be removed (but keeping the subroutine). In addition, two subroutines are required for packing/unpacking: one for e solution (one mode) and one for eAll solution (both modes). 

- 3D_MT/SolnSpace.f90 and 3D_MT/ForwardSolver.f90:
    In the 3D MT we are parallelizing over transmitters and polarizations. This why, these two modules are modified in the way that the solution structure contains now a vector (two integers) which contains the polarization index (1 or 2). In ForwardSolver.f90, I included the polarization index in the loop over nPol. The polarization index here is very important to set the correct boundary conditions.

- 3D_MT/modelParam/ModelParam_MPI.inc, 2D_MT/modelParam/ModelParam_MPI.inc:
  To make the MPI version of this code more convenient, ALL vectors, matrices or any structure are passed now among the processors using packing and unpacking method. In this case we avoid using an explicit MPI data type (i.e. MPI_REAL) in MPI_main, this is because the packed information is passed around as MPI_PACKED (what ever the original data type is).

- 2D_MT/MPI_sub.f90:
  Similar as for 3D MT, however, it contains the 2D version of e solution, nPol_MPI is set to 1 and editing e is removed.

Minor modifications:
- In the NLCG module, there is no need anymore to copy eAll from a previous solution in the MPI version. This is because the Master (who is inside the NLCG) contains eAll.
- 3D_MT/DataFunc.f90:
