The previous fix for the "Q business" hasn't resulted 
in a critical efficiency improvement. So I've added a
mandatory logical variable to Qrows which specifies
whether Q output vectors are zero or not. If zero, no
need to set them to zero - we just skip all steps that
use these vectors. This works and QmultT no longer takes
a significant amount of time (previously ~ 100 secs on
