r223 | anya | 2010-04-28 17:52:44 -0600 (Wed, 28 Apr 2010) | 29 lines

Added some careful OpenMP directives in modelOperator3D.f90.

Note that in an array A(i,j), i represents consequtive memory locations
(at least that was the standard in Fortran 77, and unlikely changed by
the compilers). So, loops like
do j = 1,N
  do i = 1,M
    A(i,j) = ...
  end do
end do
are most efficient.
Re-ordering of the loops in modelOperator3D.f90 gave another ~5% improvement.

Now, the following subroutines are parallelized (versus the time the program
used to spend on each of these before parallelization):

Maxwell  23% 
M1solve  8%
M2solve  9%
DivCgrad 5%

Have not profiled the updated (i.e., OpenMP) code yet. 

Note that automatic parallelization in Intel, PGI and XLF90_r compilers does
a good enough job that quick manual OpenMP in sg_vector.f90 actually decreases
performance, compared to automatic.

Intel compiler is by far the most impressive.

