r215 | meqbel | 2010-04-02 10:54:39 -0600 (Fri, 02 Apr 2010) | 11 lines

Avoid creating an MPI derived data type for the model parameter. 
This is because creating an MPI derived data type require using the MPI subroutine MPI_ADDRESS (MPI-1) or MPI_GET_ADDRESS (MPI-2). 
Since NOT all the clusters have MPI-2, we restrict our self to use the standard MPI-1. However, using the first subroutine causes the problem: 
'0- MPI_ADDRESS : Address of location given to MPI_ADDRESS does not fit in Fortran integer, see e.g. http://www.pgroup.com/resources/mpich/mpich126_pgi60.htm'.
The solution for now is:
- At the beginning of the program ALL processors initialize the model parameters (sigma0) and data (allData)
- During the inversion (or when distributing the model parameters), the ONLY processor who update the model parameters is the master (process ID 0).
- The master packs the updated model parameters values, which are as rscalar, in a global defined 1D vector, and distributes  ONLY this vector.
- The workers receive this vector and update the model parameter values in sigma0.
- The same situation is executed, however, visa versa, if a worker creates a model parameter and wants to send it to the master (e.g. JmultT).
     
