r211 | meqbel | 2010-03-26 12:03:28 -0600 (Fri, 26 Mar 2010) | 6 lines

Note: Running the parallel version of the code on LENZ did not work previously because: 
- In the old version of the code, all processes read the command line arguments (e.g. -I NLCG). On LENZ, However, ONLY the master (process ID 0) could read the command line arguments passed to the program, while the worker could not read these arguments. This causes the problem that the worker were not be able to find out which job is required when executing the program. Maybe there are missing libraries on the processes- I modified the parallel version so that ONLY the master reads command line arguments, creates cUserDef and finally broadcasts it to all workers.  
- When running the  parallel version of th program on LENZ, additional HIDDEN flags are passed to the program to executed it in parallel way. These  HIDDEN flags which are required by (LENZ) cluster cause the problem that the program read them as passed arguments.  
To avoid these two issues: 
- I modified the parallel version so that ONLY the master reads command line arguments, creates cUserDef and finally broadcasts it to all workers. 
- For the second issue, I modified parseArgs in UserCtrl module so that ALL additional HIDDEN flags are truncated. I used the fact that these flags begin with '-'.
