Propagating the changes made by Anna in SENS into MPI/MPI_main.f90. 
In particular affected were fwdPred, JmultT and Jmult. These three subroutines were previously implemented for multiply transmitters. These caused in the MPI-version of the code that each time we call one of these subroutine, a temporally data structure containing information of one transmitter is created (this is because, the parallelization is over transmitters). Moreover, a copy of eAll solution, containing the electric filed solution for one transmitter (both polarizations in 3D-MT), is also created temporarily and passed to the corresponding subroutines.  
With the new version of SENS, which contains now subroutines for only one transmitter (fwdPred_TX, JmultT_TX and Jmult_TX) the issues menchened above have been avioded and the MPI-version (in particular, MPI/MPI_main.f90) is now cleaner. 
Major changes in MPI/MPI_main.f90:
- Replacing fwdPred, JmultT and Jmult in  MPI/MPI_main.f90 (worker part) by fwdPred_TX, JmultT_TX and Jmult_TX.
- Removing all temporary data and eAll structures that have been used previouslly.
- Removing the corresponding part that computes Q for the 2D-MT case.

Minor changes in MPI/MPI_main.f90 and else where in the code:
- Renaming some general MPI subroutines (e.g. MPI-Initialization--> MPI-constructor) 
- Renaming MPI/MPI_decler.f90 to MPI/MPI_declaration.f90 to emphasize its meaning.
- Replacing the name of MPI_decler by MPI_declaration.f90  where is required in the code.

Some remarks to switch between the serial and parallel version of the code located in this branch (/ModEM/branches/MPI):
- The main idea is to use compiler directives inside the code at positions where a parallelization is required.
- Depending on the used complier, a PREPROCESSING flag must be used. For example -Mpreprocess when using pgf90 complier or the MPI version of it mpif90.
- To compile for a parallel version an additional information must be passed to the complier in the preprocessing stage. For example, -Mpreprocess -DMPI, where the -D flag defines what should be passed to the complier, in this case the word MPI is passed.

