Adding two MPI modules:
- MPI_decler.f90 contains public parameters required by the MPI call.
- MPI_Main.f90 contains an MPI warp of the subroutines included in the SensMatrix.f90. In addition, basic subroutines are included to e.g. distribute model, data and eAll solution whenever that required.
The basic idea in MPI_Main is to have two main tasks: Master task and Worker task. The Master task (includes various subroutines) sends jobs to workers and receives results from worker.The actual computation is done on the workers which call the subroutines in the SensMatrix.f90, however, with data structure that contains only one transmitter. This is because the current MPI-version is parallelized over periods to solve the forward modelling and inversion problem, and over periods and stations when computing the sensitivity matrix.
      
