resistivity). Note, however, that the ASCII input and output files
contain resistivity, to maintain compatibility with Randie Mackie's
format. Might want more flexibility in the future.

In particular, might want to include at least the following information 
into this particular model parameter type description:

a) RHO / SIGMA
b) LINEAR / LOGE / LOG10
c) CELL / EDGE / FACE ...  SPECTRAL?
(or, even E-CELL / H-FACE etc - i.e. mapping to the grid)
d) EARTH / EARTH+AIR

In conjunction with the grid, the combination of these four would 
provide the full identification for the model parameter. I suggest 
that we specify them all, either as separate variables or as 
a paramType string, e.g. "SIGMA LOGE EARTH H-CELL" (and use the index 
function in Fortran to fish out the necessary bits of information). 
Or, we could break this into two variables: "SIGMA LOGE", "EARTH H-CELL"... 

