r23 | anya | 2008-02-19 16:12:30 -0700 (Tue, 19 Feb 2008) | 12 lines

Hard to believe, but we have finally figured out what caused
NLCG to bomb when eAll argument is passed to JmultT. Here it is:
the pointer to modelParam in EMsoln (eAll%solns(j)%sigma) is set
(inside fwdPred(m,dHat,eAll)) to the input argument m. That input
argument in NLCG is local, and obviously gets deallocated before
we call the gradient computation. Gary's idea was that the model
input argument to fwdPred should always be floating around, but
who knew ;)
Everything is cleaned up in this commit. The next commit will
have no pointer to the model parameter in EMsoln; instead, it
will be explicitly passed to the subroutines that use it (modules
SensPDEcoeff and DataFunc).
