Reorganized input/output (just for the 2D_MT for now). 
Instead of a single IoMod.f90, created a subdirectory 2D_MT/ioMod
with a binary and an ascii version of IO subroutines. This means
that now Makefile has to be recreated if you want to change from
binary to ascii input or vice versa. This is probably the first
example of the usage of the "modularity" of this program.
Thus, to change from ascii to binary need to
1) replace 'use ioascii' with 'use iobinary' in Test2D,
2) run 'sh Configure.2D_MT; make'

Also, IO routines for modelParam are now in the ioMod. Before
Gary goes: 'Arh! NO! How could she do that?!', note that the
contents of the modelParam_t still have their private attribute,
but I have modified the subroutine create_modelParam and created
getValue_modelParam to extract the data for output. Added input
and output for Randie Mackie's ascii 2D model format. Will now
modify the data format slightly and create a nicer driver program.
